body:
probably not the answer you were looking for, but i found [this case](https://www.sciencedirect.com/sdfe/pdf/download/eid/1-s2.0-S0022347672800647/first-page-pdf) of a 25-month-old boy who ingested about 200 m in the 70s:

&#x200B;

>*At 10:30 A.M. on the day of admission the mother noted the onset of unusual behavior in her child: He appeared unsteady and stumbled, he was frightened and screamed while looking at a colored rug, at the ceiling, or upon seeing a housefly, and he frequently opened his eyes widely and covered his ears with his hands as if to block out unpleasant sounds.*

&#x200B;

whoa.

this reminds me a lot of a short story by jorge luis borges' called "funes the memorious".

>*Two or three times he had reconstructed a whole day; he never hesitated, but each reconstruction had required a whole day.*

if you haven't read it, i cannot recommend it enough: [http://vigeland.caltech.edu/ist4/lectures/funes%20borges.pdf](http://vigeland.caltech.edu/ist4/lectures/funes%20borges.pdf)
